---
import HomeLayout from '../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import CoffeeFinder from '../components/CoffeeFinder.astro';
import '../styles/journal.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<HomeLayout>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Independent coffee gear guidance</p>
          <h1>Find your espresso machine. Fast.</h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">Tell us only what you know. The Coffee Finder searches every published espresso-machine review and builds a practical shortlist around your budget, drinks, workflow, space, and experience.</p>
          <ul class="proof-row" aria-label="What Coffeedant offers">
            <li>Buyer-first reviews</li>
            <li>Real trade-offs</li>
            <li>No jargon wall</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <aside class="finder" aria-label="Coffee Finder introduction">
          <p class="finder-step">Start with one constraint</p>
          <h2>Every filter is optional.</h2>
          <p>Choose a budget, workflow, or drink style—or search the complete catalog immediately. High-end ranges now extend beyond $5,000.</p>
          <a class="finder-button" href="#coffee-finder">Open the Coffee Finder →</a>
          <p class="finder-note">No email required. Results update instantly.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="journal-home-entry" aria-labelledby="journal-home-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <div><span class="journal-label">New / Coffeedant Journal · Volume 01</span><h2 id="journal-home-title">There’s a world<br/>in your cup.</h2><p>From the coffeehouses of Süleyman’s Istanbul to the science of a sweeter Americano. Deeply researched stories, practical brewing knowledge and buying guides for the endlessly curious.</p><a href={`${base}journal/`} data-journal-home-link>Explore the Journal ↗</a><small>History · Zeitgeist · Brew Lab · Guides</small><noscript><a href={`${base}journal/`}>Read the Journal →</a></noscript></div>
        <img src={`${base}journal/history.webp`} width="1536" height="1024" alt="Original illustrated reconstruction of an Ottoman coffeehouse" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </section>
    <CoffeeFinder variant="full" />

    <section class="section guides" aria-labelledby="guides-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <span class="section-number">02 / Field guides</span>
          <h2 id="guides-title">Choose with context.</h2>
          <p>Clear comparisons for the decisions that actually change what ends up in your cup.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-grid">
          <a class="guide-card" href={`${base}espresso-machine/`}>
            <span class="guide-kicker">Start here · Buying guide</span>
            <h3>Espresso machines, decoded</h3>
            <p>Automatic, semi-automatic, single boiler, dual boiler. See what each choice means in daily use.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="guide-card" href={`${base}espresso-machine/built-in-grinder/`}>
            <span class="guide-kicker">Roundup · All-in-one</span>
            <h3>Best machines with a grinder</h3>
            <p>When the all-in-one route makes sense, and where it forces a compromise.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="guide-card" href={`${base}blog/conical-vs-flat-burr-grinders/`}>
            <span class="guide-kicker">Explainer · Grinders</span>
            <h3>Conical vs. flat burrs</h3>
            <p>A practical look at taste, workflow, retention, and value.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="guide-card" href={`${base}coffee-beans/`}>
            <span class="guide-kicker">Coffee beans · Reviews</span>
            <h3>Choose the coffee, too</h3>
            <p>Compare roast, changing origins, freshness and brew fit with research-led bean reviews.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="shell method-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">How we judge gear</p>
          <h2 id="method-title">Useful beats impressive.</h2>
          <p>A great machine is one that fits your drinks, patience, counter, and budget. Specs matter only when they improve the routine.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="method-list">
          <li><div><strong>Start with the routine</strong><span>Drink preference, volume, experience, and available time.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Translate the hardware</strong><span>Heat-up, temperature control, grinder quality, steam, and cleanup.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Name the trade-offs</strong><span>Every recommendation includes who should skip it and why.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Keep the catalog current</strong><span>The finder re-indexes every review every two weeks and incorporates current Amazon offer data where an exact listing is verified.</span></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

</HomeLayout>
